{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>So shall you say.</b> In this formulation." "<b>You saw.</b> There is a difference between what a person sees himself and what others report to him — for what others report to him, his heart may sometimes be divided from believing it (Mekhilta)." "<b>For from the heavens I spoke.</b> And another verse says ״וַיֵּרֶד ה' עַל הַר סִינַי״ (Exodus 19). A third verse comes and decides between them — ״מִן הַשָּׁמַיִם הִשְׁמִיעֲךָ אֶת קוֹלוֹ לְיַסְּרֶךָּ וְעַל הָאָרֶץ הֶרְאֲךָ אֶת אִשּׁוֹ הַגְּדוֹלָה״ (Deuteronomy 4): His glory in the heavens, and His fire and His might upon the earth. Another interpretation: He lowered the heavens and the heavens of heavens and spread them over the mountain; and so it says ״וַיֵּט שָׁמַיִם וַיֵּרַד״ (Psalms 18)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:23.656956565Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}